-- The emitter's remaining expression forms, in one exhibit.
--
-- The other five files here each pin one ruling. This one exists for coverage:
-- an adversarial review found that across all of them the harness exercised
-- `for all` and `Decimal.sum` and nothing else — no private toplevel
-- (`depends on`), no `match` over a MAYBE, no date literal or `Date.get_*`, no
-- `optional of`, no `combine all`, no `number of`, no `contains`, no
-- `impossible`, no lenient `Date`. Each of those paths could have regressed
-- with nothing in the repo noticing.
--
-- So: a small vehicle registry, whose rules reach every one of them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

DECLARE Registration HAS
    plate       IS A STRING                 -- never inspected: elided under R11
    firstOnRoad IS A DATE
    seats       IS A NUMBER
    endorsement IS A MAYBE NUMBER           -- `optional of decimal`

DECLARE Fleet HAS
    members IS A LIST OF Registration

DECLARE `Plate class` IS ONE OF
    ordinary
    vintage
    diplomatic

-- A non-exported helper: a private `declaration … depends on … equals`.
GIVEN r IS A Registration
GIVETH A NUMBER
`seat levy` r MEANS r's seats TIMES 12

-- `YMD` on literal components is a Catala date literal; the getters are the
-- `Date` stdlib module, and `count` is `number of` behind an R2 coercion.
@export The year a vehicle came onto the road, and the levy it attracts.
GIVEN f IS A Fleet
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fleet levy` f MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD `seat levy` r) (f's members))

@export Registrations are pre-2020 if they were on the road before the cutoff.
GIVEN r IS A Registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`pre cutoff` r MEANS DATE_YEAR (r's firstOnRoad) LESS THAN DATE_YEAR cutoff
  WHERE
    cutoff MEANS YMD 2020 1 1

-- `fromMaybe` is a `match` over `optional of`; the endorsement carries a
-- penalty that folds into the levy.
@export The endorsement penalty, zero when there is none.
GIVEN r IS A Registration
GIVETH A NUMBER
penalty r MEANS fromMaybe 0 (r's endorsement)

-- `foldl` is `combine all … initially … with …`; `elem` is `contains`;
-- `count` is `number of`.
@export Whether a fleet is oversized, and by how much it exceeds the cap.
GIVEN f IS A Fleet
GIVETH A NUMBER
`excess seats` f MEANS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, r YIELD acc PLUS (r's seats)) 0 (f's members) MINUS 20

@export Whether any member of the fleet seats exactly the reportable number.
GIVEN f IS A Fleet
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
reportable f MEANS
    elem 9 (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's seats) (f's members))
    AND count (f's members) GREATER THAN 0

-- `@nonexhaustive` says the author asserts the missing cases cannot arise;
-- Catala's `impossible` says exactly that, so the uncovered arms are emitted
-- rather than the CONSIDER being rejected (§2.1, §4.3).
@export nonexhaustive The registration fee for an ordinary or vintage plate.
GIVEN c IS A `Plate class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`plate fee` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
      WHEN ordinary THEN 100
      WHEN vintage  THEN 40

-- The lenient `Date day month year`, which R3 compiles through an emitted
-- day-granular helper: 31 February rolls forward.
@export The date a registration lapses: the same day, five years on.
GIVEN r IS A Registration
GIVETH A DATE
lapses r MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY (r's firstOnRoad))
         (DATE_MONTH (r's firstOnRoad))
         (DATE_YEAR (r's firstOnRoad) PLUS 5)

-- Two registrations feed the directives below:
--   SBA1234A  on the road 2018-06-01,  5 seats, no endorsement
--   SBB5678B  on the road 2021-03-15,  9 seats, 250 endorsement

#EVAL `fleet levy` (Fleet WITH members IS LIST (Registration WITH plate IS "SBA1234A", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2018 6 1, seats IS 5, endorsement IS NOTHING), (Registration WITH plate IS "SBB5678B", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2021 3 15, seats IS 9, endorsement IS JUST 250))

#EVAL `plate fee` vintage

#EVAL `pre cutoff` (Registration WITH plate IS "SBA1234A", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2018 6 1, seats IS 5, endorsement IS NOTHING)

#EVAL penalty (Registration WITH plate IS "SBB5678B", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2021 3 15, seats IS 9, endorsement IS JUST 250)

#EVAL penalty (Registration WITH plate IS "SBA1234A", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2018 6 1, seats IS 5, endorsement IS NOTHING)

#EVAL `excess seats` (Fleet WITH members IS LIST (Registration WITH plate IS "SBA1234A", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2018 6 1, seats IS 5, endorsement IS NOTHING))

#EVAL reportable (Fleet WITH members IS LIST (Registration WITH plate IS "SBB5678B", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2021 3 15, seats IS 9, endorsement IS JUST 250))

-- 29 February 2020 plus five years: 2025 has no 29 February, so the lenient
-- `Date` rolls it forward to 1 March 2025 (R3, §8.3).
#EVAL lapses (Registration WITH plate IS "SBA1234A", firstOnRoad IS YMD 2020 2 29, seats IS 5, endorsement IS NOTHING)
